EXPERIMENT 8
Date: 29-10-2026
Title: To install and configure Snort as an Intrusion Detection System (IDS), create a custom detection rule,
generate test network traffic and analyze the alerts produced by Snort.
Requirements
• Kali Linux Virtual Machine
• VirtualBox
• Snort
• Administrator privileges
Theory
An IDS monitors network traffic to detect suspicious activities and generate alerts when predefined rules match
the traffic.
Snort is an open-source network security tool used for real-time traffic analysis and intrusion detection.
Types of IDS
1. Network-Based IDS (NIDS): Monitors packets travelling through a network to detect suspicious traffic.
2. Host-Based IDS (HIDS): Monitors activities on an individual computer, such as files, processes and system
logs.
Procedure
1. Install and Verify Snort
sudo apt update
sudo apt install snort -y
snort -V
• sudo: Executes commands with administrator privileges.
• apt update: Updates the package list.
• sudo apt install snort -y: Installs Snort and automatically confirms installation.
• snort -V: Displays the installed Snort version.
2. Identify the Network Interface
ip -br addr
ip route
• ip -br addr: Displays network interfaces and their IP addresses in brief format.
• ip route: Displays routing information and the default gateway.
3. Create a Custom Rule
mkdir -p ~/snort-lab
cd ~/snort-lab
nano local.rules
Enter the following rule in local.rules:
alert icmp any any -> any any (msg:"LAB: ICMP traffic detected"; sid:1000001; rev:1;)
• alert: Generates an alert when the rule matches.
• icmp: Monitors ICMP traffic (commonly used by the ping command).
